\par \page }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 I-3. Undergraduate Class Size
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par In the table below, please use the following definitions to report information about the size of classes and class sections offered in the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid6103706\charrsid9774027 Fall}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid7743896\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid7952518 2017}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  term.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Class Sections:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027   A class section is an
 organized course offered for credit, identified by discipline and number, meeting at a stated time or times in a classroom or similar setting, and not a subsection such as a laboratory or discussion session. Undergraduate class sections are defined as an
y sections in which at least one degree-seeking undergraduate student is enrolled for credit. Exclude}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
distance learning classes and noncredit classes and individual instruction such as dissertation or thesis research, music instruction, or one-to-one readin
gs. Exclude students in independent study, co-operative programs, internships, foreign language taped tutor sessions, practicums, and all students in one-on-one classes. Each class section should be counted only once and should not be duplicated because o
f course catalog cross-listings.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Class Subsections:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
  A class subsection includes any subsection of a course, such as laboratory, recitation, and discussion subsections that are supplementary in nature and are scheduled to meet separately from the lecture p
ortion of the course. Undergraduate subsections are defined as any subsections of courses in which degree-seeking undergraduate students enrolled for credit. As above, exclude noncredit classes and individual instruction such as dissertation or thesis res
earch, music instruction, or one-to-one readings. Each class subsection should be counted only once and should not be duplicated because of cross-listings.
\par 
\par Using the above definitions, please report for each of the following class-size intervals the number of }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 class sections}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 class subsections}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  offered in}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid6103706\charrsid9774027  Fall }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid7952518 2017}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
. For example, a lecture class with 800 students who met at another time in 40 separate labs with 20 students should be counted once in the \'93100+\'94 column in the class section column and 40 times under the \'9320-29\'94
 column of the class subsections table. 
\par 
