Applicant who is offered admission to a degree-granting program}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 at your institution.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par 
\par *Adult student services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Admission assistance, support, orientation, and other services expressly for adults who have started
 college for the first time, or who are re-entering after a lapse of a few years.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9439432 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid15031900\charrsid9774027 American Indian or Alaska N}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9439432\charrsid9774027 ative: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 A person having origins in any of the original peoples of North and South America (including Central America) and maintaining tribal affilia
tion or community attachment.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9439432\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Applicant (first-time, first year): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 An individual who has fulfilled the institution\rquote s requirements to be considered for admission (including payment or waiving of the application fee, if any) and who has been notified of one o
f the following actions: admission, nonadmission, placement on waiting list, or application withdrawn (by applicant or institution).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Application fee: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 That amount of money that an institution charges for processing a student\rquote 
s application for acceptance. This amount is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 not }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
creditable toward tuition and required fees, nor is it refundable if the student is not admitted to the institution.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s48\ql \li0\ri0\sa133\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12135258 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f42\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 Asian:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 
A person having origins in any of the original peoples of the Far East, Southeast Asia, or the Indian subcontinent, including, for example, Cambodia, China, India, Japan, Korea, Malaysia, Pakistan, the Philippine Islands, Thailand, and Vietnam.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Associate degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 An award that normally requires at least two but less than four years of full-time equivalent college work.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Bachelor\rquote s degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An award (baccalaureate or equivalent degree, as determined by the Secretary of the U.S. Department of Education) that normally requires at least four years but }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 not}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  more than five years of full-time equivalent college-level work. This includes ALL bachelor\rquote 
s degrees conferred in a five-year cooperative (work-study plan) program. (A cooperative plan provides for alternate clas
s attendance and employment in business, industry, or government; thus, it allows students to combine actual work experience with their college studies.) Also, it includes bachelor\rquote 
s degrees in which the normal four years of work are completed in three years.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s48\ql \li0\ri0\sa133\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12135258 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f42\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 Black or African American}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 : }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 
A person having origins in any of the black racial groups of Africa.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Board (charges): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Assume average cost for 19 meals per week or the maximum meal plan.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Books and supplies (costs): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Average cost of books and supplies. Do not 
include unusual costs for special groups of students (e.g., engineering or art majors), unless they constitute the majority of students at your institution.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 The method by which an institution structures most of its courses for the academic year.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12546533 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid9774027 Campus Ministry:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid9774027 
 Religious student organizations (denominational or nondenominational) devoted to fostering religious life on college campuses. May also refer to Campus Crusade for Christ, an interdenominational Christian organization.
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Career and placement services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A range of services, including (often) the following: coordination of visits of employers to campus; aptitude and vocational testing; interest inventories, personal counseling; help in resume writing, interviewing, launching the job sea
rch; listings for those students desiring employment and those seeking permanent positions; establishment of a permanent reference folder; career resource materials.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Carnegie units: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
One year of study or the equivalent in a secondary school subject.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Certificate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Postsecondary award, certificate, or diploma.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Class rank: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
The relative numerical position of a student in his or her graduating class, calculated by the high school on the basis of grade-point average, whether weighted or unweighted.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 College-preparatory program: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Courses in academic subjects (English, history and social studies, foreign languages, mathematics, science, and the arts) that stress preparation for college or university study. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Common Application: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 The standard a
pplication form distributed by the National Association of Secondary School Principals for a large number of private colleges who are members of the Common Application Group. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Community service program: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Referral center for students wishing to perform volunteer work in the community or participate in volunteer activities coordinated by academic departments.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Commuter: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A student who lives off campus in housing that is not owned by, operated by, or affiliated with the college. This category includes students who commute from home and students who have moved to the area to attend college. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Contact hour: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A unit of measure that represents an hour of scheduled instruction given to students. Also referred to as clock hour.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Continuous basis (for program enrollment): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A calendar system classification that is used by institutions that enroll students at any time during the academic year. For example, a cosmetology school or a word processing school might allow students to enroll and begin studies at various times, with 
no requirement that classes begin on a certain date.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Cooperative }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid16467722\charrsid9774027 education}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  program: }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A program that provides for alternate class attendance and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid6951142\charrsid9774027 employment in business, industry, or government.}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid5328944\charrsid9774027 Cooperative housing: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid5328944\charrsid9774027 College-owned, -operated, or -affiliated hou
sing in which students share room and board expenses and participate in household chores to reduce living expenses.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Counseling service: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Activities designed to assist students in making plans and decisions related to their education, career, or personal development.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Credit: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Recognition of attendance or performance in an instructional activity (course or program) that can be applied by a recipient toward the requirements for a degree, diploma, certificate, or other formal award.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Credit course: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A course that,
 if successfully completed, can be applied toward the number of courses required for achieving a degree, diploma, certificate, or other formal award.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Credit hour: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A unit of measure representing an hour (50 minutes) of instruction over a 15-week period in a
 semester or trimester system or a 10-week period in a quarter system. It is applied toward the total number of hours needed for completing the requirements of a degree, diploma, certificate, or other formal award.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Cross-registration: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A system whereby stud
ents enrolled at one institution may take courses at another institution without having to apply to the second institution.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par Deferred admission: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 The practice of permitting admitted students to postpone enrollment, usually for a period of one academic term or one year.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An award conferred by a college, university, or other postsecondary education institution as official recognition for the successful completion of a program of studies.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Degree-seeking students: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Students enrolled in courses for credit wh
o are recognized by the institution as seeking a degree or formal award. At the undergraduate level, this is intended to include students enrolled in vocational or occupational programs.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Differs by program (calendar system): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A calendar system classificatio
n that is used by institutions that have occupational/vocational programs of varying length. These schools may enroll students at specific times depending on the program desired. For example, a school might offer a two-month program in January, March, May
, September, and November; and a three-month program in January, April, and October.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Diploma: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Postsecondary award, certificate, or diploma.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Distance learning: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 An option for earning course credit at off-campus locations via cable television, internet, sa
tellite classes, videotapes, correspondence courses, or other means.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb75\sa150\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5258716 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5258716\charrsid9774027 Doctor\rquote s degree-research/scholarship}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5258716\charrsid9774027 : A Ph.D. or other doctor's degree that requires advanced work beyond the master\rquote s level, including the preparation and defense of a dissertation based
 on original research, or the planning and execution of an original project demonstrating substantial artistic or scholarly achievement. Some examples of this type of degree may include Ed.D., D.M.A., D.B.A., D.Sc., D.A., or D.M, and others, as designated
 by the awarding institution.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5258716\charrsid9774027 Doctor\rquote s degree-professional practice}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5258716\charrsid9774027 : A doctor\rquote 
s degree that is conferred upon completion of a program providing the knowledge and skills for the recognition, credential, or license required for professional practice. The degr
ee is awarded after a period of study such that the total time to the degree, including both pre-professional and professional preparation, equals at least six full-time equivalent academic years. Some of these degrees were formerly classified as \'93
first-professional\'94
 and may include: Chiropractic (D.C. or D.C.M.); Dentistry (D.D.S. or D.M.D.); Law (L.L.B. or J.D.); Medicine (M.D.); Optometry (O.D.); Osteopathic Medicine (D.O); Pharmacy (Pharm.D.); Podiatry (D.P.M., Pod.D., D.P.); or, Veterinary Medicine (D.
V.M.), and others, as designated by the awarding institution.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5258716\charrsid9774027 Doctor\rquote s degree-other}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5258716\charrsid9774027 : A doctor\rquote s degree that does not meet the definition of a doctor\rquote 
s degree - research/scholarship or a doctor\rquote s degree - professional practice.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Double major: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Program in which students may complete two undergraduate programs of study simultaneously.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par Dual enrollment: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A program through which high school students may enroll in college courses while still enrolled in high school. Students are not required to apply for admission to
 the college in order to participate.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Early action plan: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An admission plan that allows students to apply and be notified of an admission decision well in advance of the regular notification dates. If admitted, the candidate is not committed to enroll; the student may reply to the offer under the college\rquote 
s regular reply policy.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Early admission: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A policy under which students who have not completed high school are admitted and enroll full time in college, usually after completion of their junior year.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Early decision plan: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A plan that permits students to apply and be notified of an admission decision (and financial aid offer if applicable) well in advance of the regular notification date. Applicants agree to accept an offer of admission and, if admitted, to with
draw their applications from other colleges. There are three possible decisions for early decision applicants: admitted, denied, or not admitted but forwarded for consideration with the regular applicant pool, without prejudice.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 English as a Second Language (ESL): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A course of study designed specifically for students whose native language is not English.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Exchange student program-domestic: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Any arrangement between a student and a college that permits study for a semester or more at another college}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  in the United States }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 without extending the amount of time required for a degree. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 See also Study abroad}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 .
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 External degree program:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 A program of study in which students earn credits toward a degree through independent study, college courses, proficiency examinations, and personal experience. External degree programs require minimal or no classroom attendance.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Extracurricular activities (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Special consideration in the admissions process given for participation in both school and nonschool-related activities of interest to the college, such as clubs, hobbies, student government, athletics, performing arts, etc.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 First-time student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A student attending any institution for the first time at the level enrolled. Includes students enrolled in the f
all term who attended a postsecondary institution for the first time at the same level in the prior summer term. Also includes students who entered with advanced standing (college credit earned before graduation from high school).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 First-time, first-year (freshman) student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A student attending any institution for the first time at the undergraduate level. Includes students enrolled in the fall term who attended college for the first time in the prior summer term. Also includes students who entered with advan
ced standing (college credits earned before graduation from high school).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 First-year student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A student who has completed less than the equivalent of 1 full year of undergraduate work; that is, less than 30 semester hours (in a 120-hour degree program) or less than 900 contact hours.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Freshman: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A first-year undergraduate student.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Freshman/new student orientation: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Orientation addressing the academic, social, emotional, and intellectual issues involved in beginning college. May be a few hours or a few days in length; at some colleges, there is a fee.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Full-time student (undergraduate): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A student enrolled for 12 or more semester credits, 12 or more quarter credits, or 24 or more contact hours a week each term.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Geographical residence (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Specia
l consideration in the admission process given to students from a particular region, state, or country of residence.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Grade-point average (academic high school GPA): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 T
he sum of grade points a student has earned in secondary school divided by the number of courses taken. The most common system of assigning numbers to grades counts four points for an A, three points for a B, two points for a C, one point for a D, and no 
points for an E or F. Unweighted GPA\rquote s assign the same weight to each course. Weighting gives students additional points for their grades in advanced or honors courses.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Graduate student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A student who holds a bachelor\rquote s or equivalent, and is taking courses 
at the post-baccalaureate level.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Health services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Free or low cost on-campus primary and preventive health care available to students.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 High school diploma or recognized equivalent: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A document certifying the successful completion of a prescribed secondary 
school program of studies, or the attainment of satisfactory scores on the Tests of General Educational Development (GED), or another state-specified examination.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s48\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12135258 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f42\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 Hispanic or Latino:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 
A person of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Cuban, South or Central American, or other Spanish culture or origin, regardless of race.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Honors program:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Any special program for very able students offering the opportunity for educational enrichment, independent study, acceleration, or some combination of these.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  
\par Independent study: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Academic work chosen or designed by the student with the approval of the department concerned, under an instructor\rquote 
s supervision, and usually undertaken outside of the regular classroom structure.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par In-state tuition: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 The tuition charged by institutions to those students who meet the state\rquote s or institution\rquote s residency requirements.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 International student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 See}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Nonresident alien.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid593585 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid12546533\charrsid9774027 International student group: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid593585\charrsid9774027 Student groups that facilitate cultural dialogue, support a diverse campus, assist international students in acclimation and creating a social network.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\cf2\insrsid593585\charrsid9774027 \~

\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Internship:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Any short-term, supervised work experience usually related to a student\rquote s major field, for which the student earns academic credit. The work can be full- or part-time, on- or off-campus, paid or unpaid.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Learning center: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Center offering assistance through tutors, workshops, computer programs, or audiovisual equipment in reading, writing, math, and skills such as taking notes, managing time, taking tests.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par *Legal services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Free or low cost legal advice for a range of issues (personal and other).}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Liberal arts/career combination: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Program in which a student earns undergraduate degrees in two separate fields, one in a liberal arts major and the other in a professional or specialized major, whether on campus or through cross\_registration.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb75\sa150\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid924749 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid924749\charrsid9774027 Master's degree}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid924749\charrsid9774027 : An award that requires the successful completion of a program of study of generally one or two full-time equivalent academic years of work beyond the bachelor's degree. Some of these degrees, such as those in Theol
ogy (M.Div., M.H.L./Rav) that were formerly classified as "first-professional", may require more than two full-time equivalent academic years of work. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Minority affiliation (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Special consideration in the admission process for members of designated racial/ethnic minority groups.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Minority student center: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Center with programs, activities, and/or services intended to enhance the college experience of students of color.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid12546533\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12546533 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid9774027 Model United Nations: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid9774027 A simulation activity focusing on conflict resolution, globalization, and diplomacy. Assuming roles as foreign ambassadors and \'93delegates,\'94 students co
nduct research, engage in debate, draft resolutions, and may participate in a national Model UN conference.  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s48\ql \li0\ri0\sa133\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12135258 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f42\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs21 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs21\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs21 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\fs21\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs21 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs21\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 
A person having origins in any of the original peoples of Hawaii, Guam, Samoa, or other Pacific Islands.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Nonresident alien: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A person who is not a citizen or national of the United States and who is in this country on a visa or temporary basis and does not have the right to remain indefinitely.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *On-campus day care: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Licensed day care for students\rquote  children (usually age 3 and up); usually for a fee.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Open admission: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Admission policy under which virtually all secondary school graduates or students with GED equivalency diplomas are admitted without regard to academic record, test scores, or other qualifications.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Other expenses (costs): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Include average costs for clothing, laundry, entertainment, medical (if not a required fee), and furnishings.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Out-of-state tuition: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 The tuition charged by institutions to those students who do not meet the institution\rquote 
s or state\rquote s residency requirements.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Part-time student (undergraduate): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A student enrolled for fewer than 12 credits per semester or quarter, or fewer than 24 contact hours a week each term.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Personal counseling}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
: One-on-one or group counseling with trained professionals for students who want to explore personal, educational, or vocational issues.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Post-baccalaureate certificate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 An award that requires completion of an organized program of study requiring 18 credit hours beyond the bachelor\rquote s; designed for persons who have
 completed a baccalaureate degree but do not meet the requirements of academic degrees carrying the title of master.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Post-master\rquote s certificate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An award that requires completion of an organized program of study of 24 credit hours beyond the master\rquote s degree but does not meet the requirements of academic degrees at the doctoral level.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Postsecondary award, certificate, or diploma: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Includes the following three IPEDS definitions for postsecondary awards, certificates, and diplomas of varying durations and credit/contact hour requirements\emdash 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li360\ri324\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin324\lin360\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Less Than 1 Academic Year:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  Requires completion of an organized program of study at the postsecondary level (below the baccalaureate degree) in less than 1 academic year (2 semesters or 3 quarters) or in less than 900 contact hou
rs by a student enrolled full-time.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 At Least 1 But Less Than 2 Academic Years:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Requires completion of an organized program of study at the postsecondary level (below the baccalaureate degree) in at least 1 but less than 2 full-time equivalent academic year
s, or designed for completion in at least 30 but less than 60 credit hours, or in at least 900 but less than 1,800 contact hours.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 At Least 2 But Less Than 4 Academic Years:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Requires completion of an organized program of study at the postsecondary level (be
low the baccalaureate degree) in at least 2 but less than 4 full-time equivalent academic years, or designed for completion in at least 60 but less than 120 credit hours, or in at least 1,800 but less than 3,600 contact hours.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid1211867\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid1211867\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Private institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An educational institution controlled by a private individual(s) or by a nongovernmental agency, usually supported primarily by other than public funds, and operated by other than publicly elected or appointed officials.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Private for-profit institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A private 
institution in which the individual(s) or agency in control receives compensation, other than wages, rent, or other expenses for the assumption of risk.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par Private nonprofit institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A private institution in which the individual(s) or agency in control re
ceives no compensation, other than wages, rent, or other expenses for the assumption of risk. These include both independent nonprofit schools and those affiliated with a religious organization.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Proprietary institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 See}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Private for-profit institution.
\par Public institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An educational institution whose programs and activities are operated by publicly elected or appointed school officials, and which is supported primarily by public funds.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Quarter calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 A calendar system in which the academic 
year consists of three sessions called quarters of about 12 weeks each. The range may be from {\*\xmlopen\xmlns3{\factoidname place}}10{\*\xmlclose} to 15 weeks. There may be an additional quarter in the summer.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Race/ethnicity: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Category used to describe g
roups to which individuals belong, identify with, or belong in the eyes of the community. The categories do not denote scientific definitions of anthropological origins. A person may be counted in only one group.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Race/ethnicity unknown: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Category used to cl
assify students or employees whose race/ethnicity is not known and whom institutions are unable to place in one of the specified racial/ethnic categories.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Religious affiliation/commitment (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Special consideration given in the admission 
process for affiliation with a certain church or faith/religion, commitment to a religious vocation, or observance of certain religious tenets/lifestyle. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Religious counseling: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
One-on-one or group counseling with trained professionals for students who want to explore religious problems or issues.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Remedial services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Instructional courses designed for students deficient in the general competencies necessary for a regular postsecondary curriculum and educational setting.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Required fees: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Fixed sum charged to s
tudents for items not covered by tuition and required of such a large proportion of all students that the student who does NOT pay is the exception. Do not include application fees or optional fees such as lab fees or parking fees. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Resident alien or other eligible non-citizen: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A person who is not a citizen or national of the United States and who has been admitted as a legal immigrant for the purpose of obtaining permanent resident alien status (and who holds either an alien registration card [Form I-551 o
r I-151], a Temporary Resident Card [Form I-688], or an Arrival-Departure Record [Form I-94] with a notation that conveys legal immigrant status, such as Section 207 Refugee, Section 208 Asylee, Conditional Entrant Parolee or Cuban-Haitian).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Room and board (charges)\emdash on campus: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Assume double occupancy in institutional housing and 19 meals per week (or maximum meal plan).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Secondary school record (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Information maintained by the secondary school that may include such things as the student\rquote s high school transcript, class rank, GPA, and teacher and counselor recommendations.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Semester calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A calendar system that consists of two semesters during the academic year with about 16 weeks for each semester of instruction. There may be an additional summer session.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Student-designed major: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A program of study based on individual interests, designed with the assistance of an adviser.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Study abroad:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  Any arrangement by which a student completes part of the college program studying in another count
ry. Can be at a campus abroad or through a cooperative agreement with some other {\*\xmlopen\xmlns3{\factoidname place}}U.S.{\*\xmlclose} college or an institution of another country.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Summer session: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A summer session is shorter than a regular semester and not considered part of the academic year. It i
s not the third term of an institution operating on a trimester system or the fourth term of an institution operating on a quarter calendar system. The institution may have 2 or more sessions occurring in the summer months. Some schools, such as vocationa
l and beauty schools, have year-round classes with no separate summer session.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Talent/ability (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Special consideration given to students with demonstrated talent/abilities in areas of interest to the institution (e.g., sports, the arts, languages, etc.).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Teacher certification program:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 Program designed to prepare students to meet the requirements for certification as teachers in elementary, middle/junior high, and secondary schools.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Transfer applicant: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
An individual who has fulfilled the institution\rquote 
s requirements to be considered for admission (including payment or waiving of the application fee, if any) and who has previously attended another college or university and earned college-level credit. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par Transfer student:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  A student entering the
 institution for the first time but known to have previously attended a postsecondary institution at the same level (e.g., undergraduate). The student may transfer with or without credit.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Transportation (costs): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Assume two round trips to student\rquote s hometown per year for students in institutional housing or daily travel to and from your institution for commuter students.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Trimester calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 An academic year consisting of 3 terms of about 15 weeks each.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Tuition: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Amount of money charged to students for instructional services. Tuition may be charged per term, per course, or per credit. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par *Tutoring: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 May range from one-on-one tutoring in specific subjects to tutoring in an area such as math, reading, or writing. Most tutors are college students; at some coll
eges, they are specially trained and certified.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Unit: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
a standard of measurement representing hours of academic instruction (e.g., semester credit, quarter credit, contact hour).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Undergraduate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
A student enrolled in a four- or five-year bachelor\rquote s degree program, an associate degree program, or a vocational or technical program below the baccalaureate.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Veteran\rquote s counseling: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Helps veterans and their dependents obtain benefits for their selected program and provides certifications to the Veteran\rquote s Administration. May also provide personal counseling on the transition from the military to a civilian life.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Visually impaired: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Any person whose sight loss is not correctable and is sufficiently severe as to adversely affect educational performance.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Volunteer work (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Special consideration given to students for activity done on a volunteer basis (e.g., tutoring, hospital care, working with the elderly or disabled) as a service to the community or the public in general.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Wait list: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 List 
of students who meet the admission requirements but will only be offered a place in the class if space becomes available. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Weekend college:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 A program that allows students to take a complete course of study and attend classes only on weekends. 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s48\ql \li0\ri0\sa133\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12135258 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \f42\fs24\cf1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs20\insrsid8533337\charrsid9774027 White}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 :}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 
\ltrch\fcs0 \f0\fs20\insrsid12135258\charrsid9774027 A person having origins in any of the original peoples of Europe, the Middle East, or North Africa.
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 *Women\rquote s center: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Center with programs, academic activities, and/or services intended to promote an understanding of the evolving roles of women.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Work experience (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Special consideration given to students who have been employed prior to application, whether for relevance to major, demonstration of employment-related skills, or as explanation of student\rquote 
s academic and extracurricular record.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 \page 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs24\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Financial Aid Definitions
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3755021 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid3755021\charrsid9774027 External scholarships and grants: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid3755021\charrsid9774027 Scholarships and grants received from outside (private) sources that students bring with them (e.g., Kiwanis, National Merit scholarships). The institution may process paperwork to receive the d
ollars, but it has no role in determining the recipient or the dollar amount awarded.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid3755021\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Financial aid applicant: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Any applicant who submits }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 any one of}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  the institutionally required financial aid applications/forms, such as the FAFSA. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Indebtedness: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Aggregate dollar amount bo}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid9774027 
rrowed through any loan program}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 (federal, state, subsidized, unsubsidized, private, etc.; excluding parent loans) while the student was enrolled at an institution. Student loans co-signed by a parent are assumed to be the responsibility of the student and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 should}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  be included.
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1471844 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid9774027 Institutional scholarships and grants}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid9774027 : Endowed scholarships, annual gifts and tuition funded grants for which the institution determines the recipient.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Financial need: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 As determined by your institution using the feder
al methodology and/or your institution's own standards. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Need-based aid: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
College-funded or college-administered award from institutional, state, federal, or other sources for which a student must have financial need to qualify. This includes both institutional and non}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid5141231\charrsid9774027 -}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 institutional student aid (grants, jobs, and loans).
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Need-based }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid10297048\charrsid9774027 scholarship or grant}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027  aid: }
{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Scholarships and grants from institutional, state, federal, or other sources for which a student must have financial need to qualify.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Need-based self-help aid: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Loans and jobs from institutional, state, federal, or other sources for which a student must demonstrate financial need to qualify.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Non-need-based }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid10297048\charrsid9774027 scholarship or grant}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
 aid: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Scholarships and grants, gifts, or merit-based aid from 
institutional, state, federal, or other sources (including unrestricted funds or gifts and endowment income) awarded solely on the basis of academic achievement, merit, or any other non-need-based reason. When reporting questions H1 and H2, non-need-based
 aid that is used to meet need should be counted as need-based aid. 
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Note: Suggested order of precedence for counting non-need money as need-based:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Non-need institutional grants
\par Non-need tuition waivers
\par Non-need athletic awards
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s24\ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Non-need federal grants
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li360\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Non-need state grants
\par Non-need outside grants
\par Non-need student loans
\par Non-need parent loans
\par Non-need work
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \ul\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 Non-need-based self-help aid: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid9774027 
Loans and jobs from institutional, state, or other sources for which a student need not demonstrate financial need to qualify.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid14116758\charrsid9774027 
